'''''Viola cucullata''''', the '''hooded blue violet''', '''marsh blue violet''' or '''purple violet''', is a species of the genus ''[[Viola (plant)|Viola]]'' native to eastern [[North America]], from [[Newfoundland (island)|Newfoundland]] west to [[Ontario]] and [[Minnesota]], and south to [[Georgia (U.S. state)|Georgia]].<ref>{{GRIN | access-date = 12 January 2018}}</ref> It is a recipient of the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=See RHS lists of top AGM garden-worthy plants, fruit & veg / RHS Gardening |url=http://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/trials-awards/award-of-garden-merit/agm-lists |access-date=2022-09-28 |website=www.rhs.org.uk |language=en-gb}}</ref>

== Description ==
The purple violet is a low-growing [[perennial plant|perennial]] [[herbaceous plant]] up to {{cvt|20|cm|in|0}} tall. The [[leaves]] form a basal cluster; they are simple, up to {{cvt|10|cm|in|0}} broad, with an crenate-serrate margin<ref name="Illinois Wildflowers">{{cite web |title=Marsh Violet (Viola cucullata) |url=https://www.illinoiswildflowers.info/wetland/plants/marsh_violet.html |website=Illinois Wildflowers |access-date=17 April 2025}}</ref><ref name="Ballard">{{cite web |last1=Ballard |first1=Harvey |title=Viola cucullata Aiton |url=https://people.ohio.edu/ballardh/vgpena/taxa/violacucullata.htm |website=people.ohio.edu |access-date=17 April 2025}}</ref> and a long petiole. The [[flower]]s are violet, dark blue and occasionally white. with five petals. The [[fruit]] is a [[capsule (fruit)|capsule]] {{cvt|10|–|15|mm|in|frac=8}} long, which splits into three sections at maturity to release the numerous small [[seed]]s.<ref>{{cite web |website=Northern Ontario Plant Database |url=http://www.northernontarioflora.ca/description.cfm?speciesid=1004498 |title=''Viola cucullata''}}</ref> Its habitats include wet meadows, prairies, and fields.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lady Bird Johnson Wildflower Center - The University of Texas at Austin|url=https://www.wildflower.org/plants/result.php?id_plant=vicu|access-date=|website=www.wildflower.org}}</ref><gallery>
